From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:40:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] linux-user: access_ok identity

Under identity mapping (guest_base == 0) guest pointers are host
pointers. Host heap memory (glibc malloc) is then guest memory that
QEMU never maps, so page_check_range() fails every syscall buffer in
it with EFAULT. Walk the range page by page: a page no QEMU page covers
is accepted (the host kernel checks it on access), a known page keeps
the upstream flag check, so page_unprotect() still runs for translated
guest code. A buffer straddling a known and an unknown page passes. The
walk runs under the mmap lock, since a lockless lookup can miss a mapped
page.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [identity mapping is ATL-only]
Patch-Reason: identity mapping makes host heap guest memory; QEMU cannot register every host allocation
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 linux-user/qemu.h | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/linux-user/qemu.h b/linux-user/qemu.h
index ef7aed2daec6fc71be9b9202597f05344b75d787..4ab21f39f5fb385a488ef3e1868a62c66117bd62 100644
--- a/linux-user/qemu.h
+++ b/linux-user/qemu.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "user/abitypes.h"
 #include "user/page-protection.h"
 #include "exec/page-protection.h"
+#include "exec/mmap-lock.h"
 
 #include "syscall_defs.h"
 #include "target_syscall.h"
@@ -186,12 +187,40 @@ ssize_t do_guest_readlink(const char *pathname, char *buf, size_t bufsiz);
 
 static inline bool access_ok_untagged(int type, abi_ulong addr, abi_ulong size)
 {
+    bool locked;
+    bool ok = true;
+    vaddr cur;
+    vaddr end;
+    vaddr last;
+
     if (size == 0
         ? !guest_addr_valid_untagged(addr)
         : !guest_range_valid_untagged(addr, size)) {
         return false;
     }
-    return page_check_range((target_ulong)addr, size, type);
+    if (guest_base != 0 || size == 0) {
+        return page_check_range((target_ulong)addr, size, type);
+    }
+    /*
+     * ATL identity map, page by page: a page no QEMU page covers is host
+     * memory, checked by the host kernel on access; a known page keeps its
+     * flag check (page_unprotect runs there). A range may straddle both.
+     */
+    locked = have_mmap_lock();
+    if (!locked) {
+        mmap_lock();
+    }
+    last = (vaddr)addr + size - 1;
+    for (cur = addr; ok && cur <= last; cur = end + 1) {
+        end = MIN(last, cur | ~TARGET_PAGE_MASK);
+        if (!page_check_range_empty(cur, end)) {
+            ok = page_check_range(cur, end - cur + 1, type);
+        }
+    }
+    if (!locked) {
+        mmap_unlock();
+    }
+    return ok;
 }
 
 static inline bool access_ok(CPUState *cpu, int type,
